{"schema":"LAW_EN_DOCUMENT_V1","id":"i18n-c3cf86f8f44f824713576365672587d3498997ec494de435","family_id":"KR:012159","country":"KR","language":"en","title":"Special Act on Investigating the Truth of the April 16 Sewol Ferry Disaster and Building a Safe Society","title_original":"4ㆍ16세월호참사 진상규명 및 안전사회 건설 등을 위한 특별법","kind":"법률","source_version":"284117","promulgated":null,"effective":null,"translation_status":"AI_DRAFT","body_status":"BODY_LOADED","source_url":"https://www.law.go.kr/LSW/lsInfoP.do?lsiSeq=284117","source_sha256":"c141291f23520264444e31f7c7002ae169ff7b5f49b50f81aade863d8c364da6","body_sha256":"72bd74e5e6cfb7cc3717833361d0b1fedbfd142a49d9914d9c90605fa645ac44","article_count":1,"full_text":"Article 35 (Protection of Witnesses, etc.) (1) Any witness who attends a hearing may be accompanied by counsel who is an attorney-at-law to seek advice on his/her legal rights. In such cases, the counsel shall submit a document certifying his/her qualification as an attorney-at-law. \n  (2) Where a witness or reference witness expresses his/her intention not to admit broadcasting or news photos, or requests a hearing to be held in a closed setting for any special reason, the Inquest may prohibit the recording, videotaping, broadcasting, or photographing thereof or may opt not to disclose any or all of a hearing to the public, by resolution. \n  (3) No witness, appraiser, or reference witness shall be subject to any unfavorable sanction, other than punishment prescribed by this Act, by reason of his/her testimony, appraisal, or statement at a hearing.\n","metadata":{"author_method":"Exact held-source units translated or completed using explicitly recorded source/target spans; original official records remain unchanged. All new units are MACHINE_TRANSLATION and UNREVIEWED.","author_title_record":{"path":"D:\\lawsofkorea\\projece\\07_법률번역\\06_법령별다국어완성\\LAW12_20261018_1442\\workc_1129_2094\\review_pending\\WORKC_G01_P04\\1525_KR012159\\translations\\act\\en.title.json","sha